+# self-counts.tsv — id<TAB>doc<TAB>locator<TAB>source<TAB>extract<TAB>note
+# Python regexes each have exactly one capture group: a nonnegative integer.
+# This is a reviewed population, not a digit census: exit codes, versions,
+# thresholds, line references and explicitly round-dated observations are not
+# live corpus cardinalities. SKILL.md's Falsification history is excluded by
+# its own revision-bound rule (lines 555-560); no LOG/lessons/SCORECARD history.
+# Live ledger outputs are the source of truth, never their pinned expectations.
+# R11-03 is deliberately retained because SKILL.md:36 still advertises its
+# selftest count. Its [substrate] tag MUST produce POLICY, not an OK/skip. L1
+# must resolve that declaration/scope conflict before claiming a clean gate;
+# this table cannot grant permission to execute a host/substrate row.
+SC-SKILL-STAMPS	SKILL.md	^\| Re-run a claim .*?\| .*?\(([0-9]+) stamps\b	ledger:R12-03	^([0-9]+)$	Decision table's current stamp membership; round-21 qualifier does not make the before-citing instruction historical.
+SC-SKILL-CLAIMS	SKILL.md	^\| Re-run a claim .*?\| .*?\([0-9]+ stamps \+ ([0-9]+) claims\b	ledger:R21-04	^([0-9]+)$	Decision table's total claim membership, not only the older R1 subset.
+SC-SCOPE-ROWS	SKILL.md	^\| Own vs read a shared surface .*?partitions the ([0-9]+) census rows\b	rows:corpus/surface-census.tsv	-	Current declared census row count; comments and blanks are not data.
+SC-SCOPE-SELFTEST	SKILL.md	^\| Own vs read a shared surface .*?`--selftest` proves ([0-9]+) cases\b	ledger:R16-02	^SCOPE_SELFTEST: PASS \(([0-9]+) cases\)$	Current scope gate's host-free synthetic selftest count.
+SC-SOURCES-SELFTEST	SKILL.md	^\| Learn from, cite or curate an external source .*?`--selftest` ([0-9]+) cases\b	ledger:R21-03	^SOURCES_CENSUS_SELFTEST: PASS \(([0-9]+) cases\)$	Decision table's current source-census selftest count.
+SC-CLOSURE-SELFTEST	SKILL.md	^\| closure disposition review \|.*?R24-02, ([0-9]+) cases\b	ledger:R24-02	^CLOSURE_DISPOSITIONS_SELFTEST: PASS \(([0-9]+) cases\)$	Gate registry's current closure selftest count, not a historical lesson tally.
+SC-RENDERED-SELFTEST	SKILL.md	^\| rendered-text-v1 normalizer \|.*?R24-01, ([0-9]+) cases\b	ledger:R24-01	^RENDERED_TEXT_V1_SELFTEST: PASS \(cases=([0-9]+)\)$	Gate registry's current normalizer selftest count.
+SC-LEDGER-SELFTEST	SKILL.md	^\s+bash corpus/claim-ledger\.sh --selftest # ([0-9]+) scratch cases\b	ledger:R11-09	^SELFTEST: PASS \(([0-9]+) cases\)$	Undated current command example; its old/new tail is historical, but the leading case tally is not.
+SC-CENSUS-SELFTEST	SKILL.md	^\| Exercise the handler's write-side verbs safely .*?`--selftest` proves ([0-9]+) cases\b	ledger:R11-03	^SELFTEST: PASS \(([0-9]+) cases\)$	Required decision-table case binding; BASE marks its ledger source substrate, so execution is refused pending L1 scope resolution.
